This task supplied four very different demonstrations (17x15, 9x8, 18x17, and 25x12) using unrelated palettes and visible structures, while the test was 25x19 with sparse 7 markers and long 8 borders. Several demos encoded broad spatial propagation from edge patterns and preservation of sparse anomalies; their surface forms differed substantially. The crucial durable lesson is to infer the shared coordinate/structural relation from complete input-output diffs before acting, rather than treating each returned pair as permission for another reflexive demo request. After every pair, check both transformed and unchanged regions, then make the next action only if specific competing rules remain.

In this interaction, four demo requests were issued consecutively without a substantive hypothesis update in the action turn, and the final submission extrapolated a propagation rule without showing that it fit every demo. This is a costly failure mode: demo calls consume budget, and a plausible test pattern does not validate a generator. Maintain a single ledger across all pairs, name the distinguishing evidence for any further request, and only submit after the generator and output mask pass cross-demo checks.", "file_type": ".md", "_source_path": "/home/ubuntu/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/runs/adhoc-hermesagentlearner-1792544451/attempts/07c41a7601b34a5db818bb4c02b598f2/system/state/hermes/skills/reasoning/continual-arc-demo-checkpoint/references/heterogeneous-session-review.md"}

{"success": true, "name": "continual-arc-mixed-demo-review", "file": "references/cellwise-mask-and-generator-validation.md", "content": "# Cellwise mask validation across heterogeneous demos

When an ARC task has a distinctive colored seed in noisy grids, do not equate resemblance with the rule. Track the seed shape, eligible target values, and spatial generator as independent hypotheses. For every demo, enumerate the full input/output difference mask and preserve negative evidence: unchanged lookalikes, untouched target-valued cells, and the original seed.

Before another demo or a submission, replay the proposed generator against every pair, especially when seed shape, palette, or dimensions vary. A literal translated-template matcher that looks plausible on one example but fails the varied demos is falsified; do not patch it by shifting a few cells. Request additional examples only for explicit remaining alternatives and a specific discriminating observation.", "file_type": ".md", "_source_path": "/home/ubuntu/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/runs/adhoc-hermesagentlearner-1792544451/attempts/07c41a7601b34a5db818bb4c02b598f2/system/state/hermes/skills/reasoning/continual-arc-mixed-demo-review/references/cellwise-mask-and-generator-validation.md"}

{"success": true, "name": "continual-arc-mixed-demo-review", "file": "references/seed-motif-generator-checkpoint.md", "content": "# Seed-motif generator checkpoint after a wrong submission

A salient colored seed embedded in a noisy grid does not by itself imply a copy rule. Candidate classes can include translated shape occurrences, periodic/lattice replication, directional rays, or combinations. Before extrapolating, record the seed's exact coordinates and the complete input/output difference mask in every demo. Verify both positive and negative cases: why each changed cell is selected, and why visually similar unchanged cells are excluded. Check palettes and dimensions that vary across demos; distinguish the seed color, target/background color, and unrelated noise empirically rather than assuming one role from a single pair.

After an incorrect submission, discard the whole generator. Do not move a few cells, swap a presumed background color, or switch to a nearby geometric interpretation without replaying it against every demo. With a costly attempt budget, use remaining demos for explicit competing hypotheses and only submit after a full-mask validation. Preserve all cells outside the supported transformation and verify dimensions/row lengths.", "file_type": ".md", "_source_path": "/home/ubuntu/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/runs/adhoc-hermesagentlearner-1792544451/attempts/07c41a7601b34a5db818bb4c02b598f2/system/state/hermes/skills/reasoning/continual-arc-mixed-demo-review/references/seed-motif-generator-checkpoint.md"}

